# Easter egg — level-sensitive D latch (the heart of a D flip-flop).
# When CLK=1, Q follows D; when CLK=0, Q holds its last value.
# Internally it's an SR latch with the CLK-gated S/R derived from D.
#
# Same constraint as rs-flip-flop.dcs: DCS doesn't yet evaluate
# feedback, so the would-be cross-coupling is surfaced via the
# external inputs `Q_fb` and `Qbar_fb`. In a real D latch they would
# be wired internally from Q and Qbar. Sequential primitives are
# R-9, planned for v1.3.0.

inputs: D, CLK, Q_fb, Qbar_fb
outputs: Q, Qbar

not_D = not(D)
S     = and(D, CLK)
R     = and(not_D, CLK)
Q     = nor(R, Qbar_fb)
Qbar  = nor(S, Q_fb)
